In this example, with Real and Imag parts for all fields
convergence to decent optimum using smoothing methods seems very fragile &
grid sensitive, even the very cautious Newman mode (-r)
I'm unsure how |Bx| helps here

# See data
csem1Dplotter data

# Bayes smoothing style
csem1Dinverter -v 2 -q --NS --LM -s -P --startup startup


# Smoothing methods seems quite easily deflected on other grids, e.g. --log-grid
# Creeping/Newman
csem1Dinverter -v 2 -q --NS --LM -r -P --log-grid 25 --startup startup


# But splitting seems to work pretty well in most cases
csem1Dinverter -v 2 -q --NS --LM -P --auto-split --MS d:r,5 --startup startup | grep Gridding:



# Plot profiles, or solutions
csem1Dplotter resp_final

graph -TX profile_final.txt
